# The hub broker for multi-site bridging — master subscribes here instead of any one
# site's local broker. Verified for real (see docs/architecture.md's "Multi-site
# verification" section): a genuine two-broker bridge topology, a real edge-agent
# behind the site broker, a real master behind this one, full room/reading data
# flowing through correctly, and automatic recovery after the site broker's bridge
# connection was killed and restarted — no custom retry logic needed on Canopy's
# side, this is standard Mosquitto persistent-session bridge behavior.
#
# This example is intentionally the plain/anonymous case, matching the base
# deploy/mosquitto.conf's posture — layer deploy/mosquitto.secure.conf.example's
# auth/TLS listener config on top if this hub is reachable beyond a trusted network
# (it usually is, since the whole point is accepting connections from remote sites).
listener 1883
allow_anonymous true
